# Dagric OS update channel.
#
# This is how a machine that is ALREADY INSTALLED receives fixes to Dagric
# itself. Debian's own security updates arrive through unattended-upgrades and
# never needed this; what needed it is everything in /usr/bin/dagric-*,
# /usr/share/dagric and the desktop defaults — which, until this file was
# enabled, could only ever be changed by reinstalling the operating system.
#
# The host is the download site rather than a dedicated repo.dagric.com. It is
# already on HTTPS, already deployed by the same command that publishes the
# download page, and is a name the project controls — so the channel needs no
# new infrastructure and cannot be lost with a lapsed domain.
#
# Signed by the same key that signs the ISO checksums (6CE37402BA0A0EF8), so an
# owner who verified their download is already set up to trust their updates.
#
# THIS FILE IS ONLY HALF OF IT, AND THE OTHER HALF USED TO BE MISSING.
# A source line delivers nothing unless dpkg has a record of the packages it
# serves, and for one release it had none: the four dagric-* packages were
# assembled straight into site/repo while their contents reached the ISO through
# includes.chroot, so `apt upgrade` on a sold machine could never offer a fix to
# the wizard, the manual, the wallpapers or the security baseline. build.sh now
# builds the same .debs from the tree it is about to ship and hands them to
# live-build as local packages, which is what registers them. If you ever remove
# that step, this file goes back to being decoration.
#
# WHAT ARRIVES SILENTLY AND WHAT DOES NOT. Debian's own security updates land on
# their own through unattended-upgrades. Dagric's do NOT, deliberately: the
# Origins-Pattern in 0300-hardening.hook.chroot names Debian origins only, and
# nothing there matches Origin: Dagric. So a new dagric-tools appears in Discover
# as an update the owner clicks, exactly like any other application. That is the
# intended split — "security fixes land without you having to think about it" is
# a promise worth keeping automatic; replacing the owner's own desktop tools
# behind their back is a different promise, and not one this product makes.
deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/dagric.gpg] https://dagric-os.web.app/repo trixie main
